+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                  |
+| ------ | ---------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37  |
+| Status | Draft                  |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates the caller-supplied `input` against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before the executor runs. Invalid input returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure without echoing property values; the executor is never invoked for invalid input, so the existing tool-round budget is what bounds any retry cycle.
+
+## Validation Behaviour
+
+- When `execute` receives input whose type does not match the declared schema, it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing field path without echoing the field value, and the executor is never called. ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed input without echoing its value and without calling the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L3))
